
docs/architecture/02_interfaces.md
4: **In short.** The top presents six kinds of face: class A, the MAC receive and transmit
5: byte streams; class B, the request and response contracts (`srp`, `maap`) and the read
6: faces for gPTP, AVTP, media clock and counters; class C, event strobes; class D, level
7: status wires, every one named once in F02.10; class E, the management side port; and
8: class F, the NVM port. All of them are in the one core clock domain, and every clock-domain
9: crossing, the MAC FIFOs included, is the integrator's but one: with
10: P-EN-IDENTIFY-NOTIFICATION = 1, `identify_button_i` passes the processor's own two-flop
11: synchronizer (§2 rule 3). Each class has one template
12: handshake and per-instance tables. The [integrator guide](../guides/integrator.md) is the
13: task-shaped view of the same contract.

