281: and status signals below are identical either way; no consumer can tell the
282: difference. That includes the shaper: the contract publishes the granted
283: per-source idleSlope and admission (class-D) because IEEE 802.1Q §34.3(d) makes
284: `operIdleSlope` the value "used by the credit-based shaper algorithm (8.6.8.2)
285: as the idleSlope for the corresponding queue", §34.3.2 makes SRP its sole
286: source whenever SRP is supported (§34.3(c): `adminIdleSlope` then has no
287: effect), and §34.6.1 sets a Talker's per-stream idleSlope to that stream's
288: bandwidth requirement, the per-stream value this field carries — an external
289: stack must publish the same two fields or it cannot serve this contract.
