docs/guides/hdl-engineer.md
313: |---|---|
314: | ADP advertise machine has four states, not three | [F04.2](../architecture/04_adp_engine.md#fig-04-advsm) draws DOWN / DELAY / WAITING. [`pp_adp_pkg`](../../hdl/adp/pp_adp_pkg.sv) splits the delay into its two real hardware phases: `ADP_ADV_DRAW` (the PRNG rejection sampler is running) then `ADP_ADV_DELAY` (the timer is armed). The banner records this as a deliberate refinement of the figure, and the state is externally visible — see the [operator guide](operator.md). |
315: | No dispatch ROM exists | [06 §4](../architecture/06_aecp_engine.md) specifies a dispatch ROM per opcode and [06 §8](../architecture/06_aecp_engine.md) fixes its entry shape, but no ROM and no generator ship. [`KL_aecp_engine`](../../hdl/aecp/KL_aecp_engine.sv) decodes the opcode directly, in two stages (pop, then a registered re-dispatch at the payload-walk exit), and its banner records that as a documented choice ([06 §8.1](../architecture/06_aecp_engine.md)). |
316: | The transaction record has four origins; dispatch carries one | [03 §4](../architecture/03_packet_engine.md) keeps the RX / TIMER / SELF / MGMT origin field, and the normalizer has a producer port for each, but the top stamps RX alone: expiries reach their owners on the timer's expiry bus, AECP unsolicited responses (IDENTIFY_NOTIFICATION among them) are the engine's own SELF jobs on TX lane 1, and there is no MGMT producer. [03 §5](../architecture/03_packet_engine.md#5-origins-originator-and-event-router) now states this landed shape; the three ports stay tied off. |
317: | The descriptor image is not on chip | Two places still show it inside the on-chip RAM complex: the rendered F03.1 figure, which says so under the image, and the `P-DESCR-IMAGE-BYTES` parameter, which has no consumer in the RTL. The current truth is [07 §3.3](../architecture/07_memory_maps.md) and diagram 22. |
